    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and practical problems—it’s both challenging and strangely liberating. While it’s not my strongest subject, I’ve always enjoyed the logic and precision of solving puzzles, whether in algebra or calculus. It’s satisfying when you finally crack something complex, even if I still struggle with proofs or advanced topics.",
